, "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVjanPQl", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 16, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8892917, "raw_content": "", "author": "Toobigtorig1234", "created": 1792359129463, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "www.powermentor.org", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVjanPQl.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://www.powermentor.org/blog/the-far-left-network-behind-frances-student-protest-narrative", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Follow the money--:  American activist-investor Neville Roy Singham has been linked funding the riots in France ..", "last_comment_created": 1792359129463, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 0, "score_up": 16, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": " Fifteen student and youth organizations. Thirty-five other organizations. That breakdown is the starting point for understanding the network behind the unrest in France examined by Fox News Digital\u2019s Asra Nomani. Of the 50 organizations she identified, just 30 percent were student or youth groups. The remaining 70 percent included labor unions, political parties, and other adult organizations, many she identified as communist, socialist, or far left.  Calling this simply a student uprising leaves the public with an incomplete picture of who was involved. Young people\u2019s concerns may provide the movement\u2019s public face, while established political organizations bring their own agendas, infrastructure, and ambitions. The accountability question is straightforward: Who is speaking for students, and who is using students to advance a separate political project? ", "large_image": "BcqvUznTDrY2FSHn.png", "title": "The Far Left Network Behind France\u2019s Student Protest Narrative"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVjall8X", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 58, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8892315, "raw_content": "", "author": "VanillaCupCake", "created": 1792332402881, "profile_picture": "skHhaQnk6Zfk", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Mungo", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVjall8X.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/6xj8oEfTQZix.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/w5mq3pUdnaAnmyZK.jpeg", "width": 768, "content-type": "jpeg", "height": 615}], "blurhash": "UZI|gr0$NGjY}=IqWUWBpKxZaKWC0gxsnif6", "full_resolution": [1122, 1402]}, "title": "THANK YOU GOD FOR THIS BEAUTIFUL MORNING...", "last_comment_created": 1792334551531, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 1, "score_up": 58, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVjanPMf", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 15, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8892909, "raw_content": "Can you see it? Across the country, french citizens gather around their televisions. Conversations stop. Someone turns up the volume. macron is about to speak.\r\n\r\nThe anticipation must have been palpable. Finally, some answers. A plan. Something.\r\n\r\nHe begins.\r\n\r\nMinutes go by. The concerned smiles slowly disappear. Brows furrow. A man lowers his coffee without taking a sip. A woman looks at her husband. He looks back at her.\r\n\r\nNeither says a word.\r\n\r\nmacron continues. The expressions have now progressed from cautious optimism to \u201cWhat the fuck is he talking about?\u201d\r\n\r\nAt last, he signs off.\r\n\r\nFor a moment, the french people sit in silence, staring at their screens. Then comes that rare moment of national unity. Different lives. Different politics. One shared realization.\r\n\r\nWE'RE FUCKED.", "author": "Agent_86", "created": 1792358726471, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Agent_86", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Watch french Citizens As macron Speaks. Priceless. ", "last_comment_created": 1792360799107, "content": "<p>Can you see it? Across the country, french citizens gather around their televisions. Conversations stop. Someone turns up the volume. macron is about to speak.</p>\n<p>The anticipation must have been palpable. Finally, some answers. A plan. Something.</p>\n<p>He begins.</p>\n<p>Minutes go by. The concerned smiles slowly disappear. Brows furrow. A man lowers his coffee without taking a sip. A woman looks at her husband. He looks back at her.</p>\n<p>Neither says a word.</p>\n<p>macron continues. The expressions have now progressed from cautious optimism to \u201cWhat the fuck is he talking about?\u201d</p>\n<p>At last, he signs off.</p>\n<p>For a moment, the